So the angles in a convex quadrilateral sum to \(360^\circ\). Let the smallest angle be \(x\). Then the largest angle is \(2x\). The other two angles are both \(90^\circ\). So the equation is \(x + 90 + 90 + 2x = 360\). Simplifying, we get \(3x + 180 = 360\). Solving for \(x\), we get \(3x = 180\), so \(x = 60\). The largest angle is \(2x = 2 \cdot 60 = 120^\circ\). Therefore, the largest angle is \(\boxed{120}\) degrees.
