solution_str:
\text{Given:}
\begin{align*}
&3 \text{ inches} = 10 \text{ miles} \\
&\text{Real life distance} = 53.25 \text{ miles}
\end{align*}
To find the map distance for the real life distance of $53.25$ miles, we set up a proportion based on the given ratio:
\begin{equation*}
\frac{3 \text{ inches}}{10 \text{ miles}} = \frac{x \text{ inches}}{53.25 \text{ miles}}
\end{equation*}
Cross-multiplying gives us:
\begin{equation*}
10x = 3 \times 53.25
\end{equation*}
\begin{equation*}
10x = 159.75
\end{equation*}
\begin{equation*}
x = \frac{159.75}{10}
\end{equation*}
To express $x$ as a fraction, we simplify the decimal:
\begin{equation*}
x = \frac{15975}{1000}
\end{equation*}
\begin{equation*}
x = \boxed{\frac{639}{40}}
\end{equation*}
The distance between the buildings on the map would be $\frac{639}{40}$ inches, expressed as a fraction.

\boxed{ños \begin{equation*} \end{equation*}}

